        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-20T22:14:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this needs some work to be ready, but I do think we need some intervention here to solve this latency problem.\n\nWhen it is ready, we\u0027ll probably want to do something like this in the main TCPCI driver and not just for this one TCPC.",
      "revId": "168d46c021c044d241f3b800dc871b55dd9e3e0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "463a0777_29c1c458",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/raa489000.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 351,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-20T22:14:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are not all of the requirements for entering BIST test mode. The BIST message type has to be BIST Test Mode (and not one of the other BIST modes). But also, VBUS has to be within vSafe5v.\n\nMaybe more fundamentally, the BIST message needs to arrive at a time that makes sense from a protocol POV, i.e. the port has started PD communication, is in an explicit contract, and is not in the middle of an uninterruptible AMS.\n\nThe PE is well positioned to check all of these things (see `pe_bist_tx_entry`), and the TCPC driver isn\u0027t. All of these checks are required by the PD spec. Some of them are required to pass other compliance tests.\n\nAs it stands, there\u0027s a risk that the TCPM could enter BIST mode incorrectly, and there\u0027s also a risk that the TCPC could get out of sync with the TCPM, if the TCPC driver and the PE evaluate this message differently.",
      "revId": "168d46c021c044d241f3b800dc871b55dd9e3e0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9659c43_e6d83533",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/raa489000.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 351,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T21:25:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it might prove fruitful to have a common PD function that takes a message as an argument and returns whether it is a BIST test data message, rather than trying to keep separate logic in the PE and here to do the same thing.",
      "parentUuid": "463a0777_29c1c458",
      "revId": "168d46c021c044d241f3b800dc871b55dd9e3e0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ada0ee21_26f6ff71",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/raa489000.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 351,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-19T18:36:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e about first question, I use the pe_src_ready_run condition to identified the BIST message. https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c;l\u003d2911?q\u003dpe_src_ready_run\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch,\n\nThe [logic](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c;l\u003d2967;drc\u003d1903d805d7568b3bd5e150dcb7ddff2abd94c08b) in `pe_src_ready_run`, copied here, checks if a message is a BIST message. There is also logic in `pe_bist_tx_entry` to [check the message\u0027s BIST mode](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c;l\u003d5725;drc\u003d1903d805d7568b3bd5e150dcb7ddff2abd94c08b) (copied here) and to [check that VBUS is valid for entering BIST mode](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c;l\u003d5708;drc\u003d1903d805d7568b3bd5e150dcb7ddff2abd94c08b) (not copied here).\n\nWhat I\u0027m suggesting is that rather than try to replicate the VBUS check here to match the one in `pe_bist_tx_entry`, we should refactor the code to have a single function to check VBUS and call it here.\n\nIdeally, we could have a single function called at this location to identify a BIST test data message and check VBUS. Even more ideally, that function would be called here and in the PE. However, that would require a larger refactor and might make the surrounding PE code harder to read.\n\nI\u0027d say the code structures that seem the most maintainable to me are probably\n1. A single function to check that VBUS is valid for BIST, called both here and in the PE. This could be something like `bool pd_vbus_valid_for_bist(int port);`.\n2. The PE code stays otherwise the same, with `pe_src_ready_run` checking the message type and `pe_bist_tx_entry` checking the BIST mode.\n3. A function in this driver (for now) that checks the message type and BIST field directly and also checks `pd_vbus_valid_for_bist`. That could be something like `static bool raa489000_tcpm_should_enter_bist_mode(int port, uint32_t header, uint32_t bdo);`.\n4. `raa489000_tcpm_get_message_raw` calls `raa489000_tcpm_should_enter_bist_mode(port, hdr, payload[0])` here.",
      "parentUuid": "a9659c43_e6d83533",
      "revId": "168d46c021c044d241f3b800dc871b55dd9e3e0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
