      "writtenOn": "2024-09-20T22:14:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, the effect of calling `tcpci_set_bist_test_mode` here is to do it in the PD interrupt task, rather than waiting for the PD interrupt task to signal the PD task, which will run the PE to process the message. This basically makes `pe_bist_tx_entry` a no-op.\n\nThere are some potential problems with this, and it\u0027s not my favorite way to do it (see above comment).\n\nWhat is the BIST entry latency with and without this function? Could you get a similar reduction by reducing downtime in the PD-interrupt-task to PD-task-event to PE-BIST-entry chain? The latter would be my preferred solution. For instance, could you check for BIST message type here, and then set a flag that triggers higher-priority event handling in the PE (a mechanism we\u0027d need to create)?",
      "revId": "168d46c021c044d241f3b800dc871b55dd9e3e0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "14e67602_b3424273",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/raa489000.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 353,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-19T18:36:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e for the second question, we set bist mode at the first BIST message, but before at PE stage, EC will set the bist mode at the second BIST message.\n\nCan you elaborate on this? Before this change, the first message should have ultimately caused the PE to put the TCPC in BIST mode, although the second message may have arrived by the time that happened. IIUC, this change just decreases the latency of putting the TCPC in BIST mode in response to the first message.\n\nWhat I\u0027m asking is, did you measure the components of the latency between receiving the first BIST message and entering BIST test mode? If so, what were the components of that latency? How much time does the context switch from the PD interrupt task (this function) to the PD task (`pe_bist_tx_entry`) take?\n\nIf you didn\u0027t take those measurements, that\u0027s OK, but I\u0027ll need to solve this problem in general for other TCPCs, so I\u0027d be interested in any measurements you took.",
      "parentUuid": "c59c39b3_dbca8b3b",
      "revId": "168d46c021c044d241f3b800dc871b55dd9e3e0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
